arch=x86
vmlinux_btf=7.0 kernel BTF dump (bpftool btf dump file /sys/kernel/btf/vmlinux format c, Ubuntu 24.04.5, 7.0.0-42-generic)
clang=Ubuntu clang version 18.1.3 (1ubuntu1)
load_verified=bpftool prog loadall, Ubuntu x86_64 7.0.0-42-generic, all 14 programs pinned;
  the provider's kernel tests also pass with it on AlmaLinux 8.10 (4.18.0-553),
  CentOS Linux 8.5 (4.18.0-348), Amazon Linux 2 (5.10), Amazon Linux 2023 (6.1),
  Ubuntu 20.04 (5.15 HWE), openSUSE Leap 16.0 (6.12) and Ubuntu 26.04 (7.0).
notes=rebuilt because include/rt_event_contract.h changed (a comment only);
  bpf/rt_file.bpf.c is unchanged, and the object has the same 8 program
  sections and 14 programs as the one it replaces. The header moved from 6.17
  to 7.0, the portable direction per prebuilt/README.md: CO-RE resolves offsets
  against the running kernel. Current size is recorded in the check_files
  manifests.
